    "body": "Slow-loris finding fixed in 936954e7:\n- **Fix:** `serve_client` reads the socket directly in ≤8 KiB chunks. Each read's timeout is min(poll step, remaining idle time), and the idle deadline is checked after every chunk. A partial line never resets the clock, and the 16 MB cap still holds.\n- **New test:** `a_trickling_client_is_dropped_on_the_idle_schedule`: `{` every 10 ms against a 400 ms window is dropped on schedule and logged by name, and the next client is served. It failed before the fix.\n- **Gate:** mcp_live passes 10/10 three runs in a row; mcp and mcp_setup pass; clippy is clean.\n- **Decision note:** updated.",
